# What EAS Build uploads.
#
# ⚠⚠ THIS FILE REPLACES EVERY .gitignore, IT DOES NOT ADD TO THEM. Expo's docs
# are explicit: "if it is present, none of the existing .gitignore files will be
# respected by EAS CLI." Anything missing here gets uploaded — including
# node_modules (2 GB) and, far worse, signing keys and env files. Read the whole
# file before changing one line of it.
#
# Why it exists: the RN app lives in `mobile/`, but EAS archives from the GIT
# ROOT, so every build uploaded the Next.js web app, the Swift app in `ios/`,
# and ~230 MB of avatar source art in `assets/` — 610 MB and 12m 24s of upload
# for a build that opens none of it. EAS flagged the size itself.
#
# ⚠ NO NEGATION PATTERNS. The first version of this file was a whitelist:
# `/*` to drop the repo root, then `!/mobile/` to re-admit the app. Simulated
# locally against the same `ignore` package EAS uses, that produced 449 files
# and 51 MB — correct. EAS uploaded 80 BYTES and the build errored with an empty
# archive, because it tests directory paths by a different convention and the
# trailing slash on the negation never matched, so the whole tree was pruned.
#
# A blacklist cannot fail that way: every rule is an exclusion, nothing depends
# on a later rule rescuing an earlier one. It is more lines and they are duller,
# and that is the point.
#
# ⚠ NOT SUPPORTED WITH `"requireCommit": true` in eas.json, which switches EAS
# to `git clone` and ignores this file entirely. It is not set today; if it ever
# is, this file silently stops working and the 610 MB comes back.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies and build output, at any depth. The build server installs from
# mobile/package-lock.json, so node_modules is ~2 GB of pure waste.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules
.git
.next
.turbo
.expo
web-build
dist
out
coverage
build
.remotion
.remotion-public
.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⚠ SECRETS. These were excluded only because the .gitignore files said so, and
# those are no longer read. Losing a line here uploads a signing key.
#
# ⚠ `.npmrc` IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE — mobile/.npmrc points at the Hugeicons
# private registry and the build FAILS without it. It holds no secret: the token
# is an ${ENV_VAR} reference, supplied by EAS at build time.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env*
*.pem
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
.mcp.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The repo root — the web app, the Swift app, and the art. A LEADING SLASH on
# every one of these, so `mobile/app`, `mobile/lib`, `mobile/components`,
# `mobile/assets` and `mobile/scripts` are untouched. Dropping a slash here
# deletes half the RN app from the archive.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/app
/components
/lib
/hooks
/public
/assets
/ios
/drafts
/remotion
/memory
/scripts
/skills
/.claude
/.preview-emails

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local noise.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.orig.*
.metro-health-check*
*-debug.log
*.log
